Z||000000||MooCow||02-06-2001||10:41 PM||||Hey I am going into Web design and I was offered a job today but had to reject it cause this is my first HTML class at Baker college.  I need to know how to make a web site secure?  To be able for someone to type a name in and a password and have it be secured.  Can anyone help me on this? <P>                               Thanks Ken <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||tgowens||02-07-2001||12:24 AM||||Ken, you can secure a site by using the secure folder feature on most servers........it will allow you to specify that "index.html" is secure and require a user ID and password to be entered to gain access -- you can look at the CFOG site -  <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A>  members only section for an illustration of what I am talking about -- in this manner you can assign a userID and password or require each user to notify you of their desired userID and password - at any rate, it gives the webmaster or site administrator the control of who has access...<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">    </A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||02-07-2001||12:25 AM||||oh, the other method involves a "secure server" which is a tad more complicated and more expensive - you can get more information on the VeraSign web site...<P>Hope this helps..........||||reg||1
