Z||000006||btoth||02-09-2001||11:03 AM||||Under UNIX (or Linux) you use .htpasswd and .htaccess files in the root directory of your web folder.  I believe that this works for Windows too (if you're using the Apache Web Server).  These files make it so that you have to login when you access any of the site's pages the first time you view them and it uses standard unix encryption so it's pretty secure.  My "Webmaster in a Nutshell" book (by O'Reilly) explains how to do it.||||reg||1
